NAME
       stat, fstat - get file status

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/stat.h>

       int stat(const char *path, struct stat *st);
       int fstat(int fd, struct stat *st);

DESCRIPTION
       Fills ST with the size, type, mode, owner and timestamps of a
       file, named by path or by an open descriptor.

       The type is tested with S_ISREG, S_ISDIR, S_ISLNK, S_ISCHR and
       S_ISBLK.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, -1 with errno set.

ERRORS
       ENOENT   the path does not exist
       EBADF    fd is not open
       EFAULT   st points outside the address space

SEE ALSO
       open(2), chmod(2), stat(1)
